Hi All,

I have an RSA key successfully generated by TPM.
I have been using it for hash and ticket generation, signature creation and=
 verification with SHA2_256 algorithm.

The problem occurs, if I try to use the same key with the SHA1 algorithm in=
stead of  SHA2_256.
Hash and ticket generation  works fine, validation  ticket is generated.
If my theory is correct, only "hashAlg" parameter of Tss2_Sys_Hash( ) has t=
o be set to  TPM_ALG_SHA1.
Doing the same for Tss2_Sys_Sign, operation always fails. This is the point=
 I got stuck.

I get back TPM_RC_SCHEME error code, however scheme is configured to
TPM_ALG_RSASSA and details.rsassa.hashAlg is set to TPM_ALG_SHA1.

I suspect that some parameters  need to be configured  but no idea how to p=
roceed.

Can someone give me a pointer?


